ath10k: do not reset the TXBF vdev param after VDEV_DOWN on WCN3990

For the sdm660-mainline 7.2.y kernel (tested on v7.2.3-sdm660, Xiaomi Redmi
Note 7 "lavender", WCN3990 firmware "qmi fw_version 0x101a832b", build
2020-12-21).

On every disassociation ath10k_bss_disassoc() sends WMI_VDEV_DOWN and then
ath10k_mac_vif_recalc_txbf() writes the TXBF vdev param (param 45, value 0)
to the vdev that is already down. This firmware asserts on it and takes the
whole modem down:

  ath10k_snoc 18800000.wifi: wmi tlv vdev down
  ath10k_snoc 18800000.wifi: wmi tlv vdev 0 set param 45 value 0x0
  qcom-q6v5-mss 4080000.remoteproc: fatal error received:
      err_qdi.c:459:EX:wlan_process:1:WLAN RT:4084:PC=b00ca330
  ath10k_snoc 18800000.wifi: firmware crashed!

After that the modem restarts and Wi-Fi does not come back until the radio
is switched off and on. Roaming between two APs of the same network, losing
the signal and shutting down all hit it.

Skip the reset for WCN3990 station vdevs. The param is written again by
ath10k_bss_assoc() on the next association.

The TXBF hint comes from a comment by SudosuBash in
https://github.com/sdm660-mainline/linux/issues/243

Apply with: git apply kernel-7.2/0001-ath10k-wcn3990-sem-txbf-apos-vdev-down.patch
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
index 0558041e3..4c0ba9257 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -3207,7 +3207,16 @@ static void ath10k_bss_disassoc(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 
 	arvif->def_wep_key_idx = -1;
 
-	ret = ath10k_mac_vif_recalc_txbf(ar, vif, vht_cap);
+	/* The WCN3990 firmware of SDM630/SDM660 (WLAN.HL.1.0) asserts in
+	 * wlan_process when the TXBF vdev param is written to a station vdev
+	 * that is already down, taking the whole modem down with it. The
+	 * param is set again on the next association, so skip the reset.
+	 */
+	if (ar->hw_rev == ATH10K_HW_WCN3990 &&
+	    vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)
+		ret = 0;
+	else
+		ret = ath10k_mac_vif_recalc_txbf(ar, vif, vht_cap);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath10k_warn(ar, "failed to recalc txbf for vdev %i: %d\n",
 			    arvif->vdev_id, ret);
